  "answer": "Requests accepts Unicode hostnames and converts them to ASCII using IDNA (punycode) before sending the request. In `PreparedRequest.prepare_url`, a bytes URL is first decoded as UTF-8 and other URL objects are converted to strings. The URL is parsed, and if the hostname contains non-ASCII characters, `_get_idna_encoded_host()` encodes it. Invalid IDNA labels raise `InvalidURL`. ASCII hostnames beginning with `*` or `.` are also rejected. The hostname is then reconstructed into the URL, while the path, query, and fragment are requoted as needed. For example, `https://münich.example/` becomes an URL using an IDNA hostname such as `https://xn--mnich-kva.example/`. Proxy bypass checks use the parsed hostname separately, and redirect `Location` headers are reinterpreted from Latin-1 to UTF-8 before being followed.",
